# End-of-line normalization.
#
# Strategy: normalize ALL text files to LF in the repository AND in working
# trees (`eol=lf`). The repo is already LF-only; this file makes that
# deterministic for every contributor, OS and tool, instead of depending on
# each machine's core.autocrlf setting. It also keeps the Node scripts and
# Markdown content byte-identical on Windows and Unix.
#
# Alternative: use `* text=auto` (without `eol=lf`) if you prefer Windows
# contributors to get CRLF working trees while the repo stores LF.

# Normalize text files; check them out as LF everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files that must never be touched by EOL conversion or diffs.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.avif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.eot binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip binary

# Git for Windows may guess wrong on these — pin them explicitly.
*.mjs text eol=lf
*.astro text eol=lf
*.ts text eol=lf
*.css text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf
